uerySelectorAll()` in the Plugin API (type/id/class/attribute selectors, `>` child, ` ` descendant, `+`/`~` sibling combinators, `:not` / `:is` / `:has` / `:where` / `:first-child` / `:nth-child` / `:empty`, etc). Attribute predicates support the full dot/index/`*` path grammar \u2014 `[fontSize=18]`, `[fills.0.color.r=1]`, `[mainComponent.name=Button]` all resolve through the Plugin API surface. Required when `format` is "json".'),M=n.z.number().int().min(0).max(32).describe("How deep to walk below each matched root. 0 (default) returns only the matched roots. 1 returns roots + direct children. Max 32. When depth > 0, each non-root node in the response also carries `rootId`, `depth`, and `parentId` so callers can reconstruct the tree."),j=n.z.array(n.z.string().min(1).max(256)).max(64).describe('Field paths to project onto each visited node \u2014 dot for nested properties, numeric index for array elements, `*` for "any element". Each path is its own string in the array. Examples: `name`, `characters`, `fontSize`, `width`, `height`, `children`, `parent`, `fills.0.color.r`, `mainComponent.name`, `absoluteBoundingBox.x`. Dotted/index/wildcard paths reconstruct nested structure in the output: `values: ["fills.0.color.r"]` emits `{ id, fills: [{ color: { r: 0.5 } }] }` \u2014 NOT a flat `"fills.0.color.r"` key. Projection reads through the Plugin API surface, so any documented Plugin API node property works. Bare-key projection of node refs (`["mainComponent"]`, `["parent"]`, `["children"]`) returns a stable `{id, type, name}` summary per node, never a recursive dump of internal state \u2014 descend (e.g. `["mainComponent.name"]`) for scalars. A path that resolves to `undefined`/`null` at the leaf emits `null`; descent through a missing intermediate omits the key entirely. The output object is id-only by default; list `name`, `type`, etc. explicitly here to get them back. Max 64 paths, each up to 256 chars.'),U=n.z.number().int().min(1).max(1e3).describe("Hard cap on t